nd better hands (like a Jack or pocket pair 77+) will call or raise.\n\nReason: You are currently in the lead regarding the cumulative score. Since the pot is small and your hand has showdown value but is easily beaten by a Jack or Queen, checking is the best strategy to minimize variance. It allows you to get to the showdown for free, potentially winning against Ace-high or small pocket pairs, without risking chips against a slow-played monster or a better two-pair.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
